==========================================================================
  p_rr / Lambda^4 = f(K) - f'(K) (d_r phi)^2 / Lambda^4 = f - 2 K f'

   sqrt(K)   p_rr/Lam^4
     0.000    -1.000000
     0.100    -1.002273
     0.500    -1.172041
     1.000    -1.886294
  [PASS] S4 [THE PRESSURE] at K = 0 the pressure is -1 (w = -1), and the radial
      pressure becomes MORE negative as the gradient grows
         measured: p_rr/Lambda^4: -1.0000 at K=0 -> -1.8863 at K=1
         The static configuration carries TENSION along the gradient, not
